          <change when="2024-01-11T15:11:17-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Had contacted H. Cuvigny about lin2. She stated that the proposed reading "is right".</change>
          <change when="2024-01-11T13:49:11-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">Vote - AcceptText - I totally agree with  ἐν Κόπτο -- the epsilon of ἐν looks much like that of ἐκ at the beginning of line 3. I'm also willing to accept χάρειν in line 2.</change>
          <change when="2024-01-11T12:24:25-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/j.lougovaya.ast">Vote - AcceptText - I agree with correction in l.8, but am not sure about that in l. 2.</change>
          <change when="2023-12-18T06:46:41-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Corrections in lines 2 and 8</change>
          <change when="2023-12-18T06:46:23-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - I've added a correction to line 2, where χάρειν = χαίρειν and have disentangled the beginning of line 8 as σου ἐν Κόπτο. The concave bottom part of the epsilon (instead of an alpha) can be seen, with its lower tip just above the delta of οἶδες in the next line.</change>
